{"ticker":"GLAXO","symbol":"GLAXO","instrumentId":3022671,"name":"Glaxosmith. Pharma.","industry":"NSE-Medical-Diversified","about":"GlaxoSmithKline Pharmaceuticals Ltd. is a leading pharmaceutical company in India, specializing in the manufacturing, distribution, and trading of prescription medicines and vaccines. Its product portfolio covers a wide range of therapeutic areas, including anti-infectives, dermatology, gynecology, diabetes, cardiovascular, and respiratory diseases. The company's vaccines help prevent various infectious diseases such as hepatitis A and B, influenza, chickenpox, diphtheria, cervical cancer, and more. GlaxoSmithKline Pharmaceuticals has a strong presence in India and globally. With a focus on improving health outcomes, it provides innovative and effective medical solutions to a broad spectrum of patients.","website":"www.gsk-india.com","location":"Mumbai, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:22:22.538Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":2713.4,"changePct":2.850428322341001,"week52High":3106.4,"week52Low":2103.2},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹45,967 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹4,159 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"42,351,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"329"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"22,410,477"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"2.10%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"20.27"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.8"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"—"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"0.04"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.57"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"3%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"40.09"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"14–66"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"45.7%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"53.32"},{"label":"Volume","value":"78,675"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"85,925"},{"label":"Master score","value":"58"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"49"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"64"},{"label":"Group rank","value":"29"},{"label